{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132142,"nonce":"u9OFwGLsl5pcX64aQQJ8F5CQq4s=","message":"GATE LIFTED — the catalog.py glyph cross-check that was listed as blocking\n3.2/3.3's viewport UX is done (session 4), and it does not gate you.\n\nFull write-up is on 2.5 (f7b6207). Short version: baseviz's `catalog.py` emits a\n2-char uppercase token keyed on defName for a COLOURED PNG cell; AutoRimmer's\n`CropRenderer` emits 1 ASCII char keyed on def properties for a text grid with\nno colour to disambiguate with. Different media, opposite constraints, nothing\nto reconcile — and AutoRimmer reads no catalog data at all (three comments, no\ncode). The residual hazard is two visual channels with two alphabets, which is\n2.5's to handle, not yours.\n\nYou consume `map-view`'s ASCII, which is self-consistent and, since 2.6, has an\nenforced reserved band for pawns and fog (`? @ $ ! \u0026 ^ ;`, `?` = fogged). Read\nthe glyph policy from the comment block at the top of `CropRenderer` in\n`Source/AutoRimmer/Spatial.cs` — NOT from 2.3's closing comment, whose glyph\ntable predates 2.6 and is stale on exactly those characters.","files":null}]}